{"name":"Tilled Earth","hex":"#80624e","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"tilled","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["simple past and past participle of till"]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["ploughed or cultivated"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tilled"},{"term":"earth","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["Alternative letter-case form of Earth (“the third planet of the Solar System, upon which humans live”)."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Soil.","Any general rock-based material."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/earth"}],"entries":[{"title":"Tilled Earth","blocks":[{"text":"Tilled Earth: Stories is an anthology of short stories by Manjushree Thapa. It was published in 2007 by Penguin India. It is her first short story collection and fourth book. The book was launched by poet Wayne Amtizis and filmmaker Kesang Tseten in the British Council Nepal. The book consists of twenty-one short stories."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/e/eb/Tilled-Earth.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tilled_Earth","wikidata":"Q109941543"},{"title":"Tillage","blocks":[{"text":"Tillage is the agricultural preparation of soil by mechanical agitation of various types, such as digging, stirring, and overturning. Examples of human-powered tilling methods using hand tools include shoveling, picking, mattock work, hoeing, and raking. Examples of draft-animal-powered or mechanized work include ploughing, rototilling, rolling with cultipackers or other rollers, harrowing, and cultivating with cultivator shanks (teeth)."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2e/Tillage.jpg/330px-Tillage.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tillage","wikidata":"Q878333"},{"title":"Earth","blocks":[{"text":"Earth is the third planet from the Sun and the only astronomical object known to harbor life. This is made possible by Earth being an ocean world, the only one in the Solar System sustaining liquid surface water. Almost all of Earth's water is contained in its ocean, which covers 70.8% of Earth's crust. The remaining 29.2% of Earth's crust is dry land, which is predominantly located within Earth's land hemisphere in the form of continental landmasses. Most of Earth's land is at least somewhat humid and covered by vegetation, while large ice sheets at Earth's polar deserts retain more water than Earth's groundwater, lakes, rivers, and atmospheric water combined. Earth's crust consists of slowly moving tectonic plates, which interact to produce mountain ranges, volcanoes, and earthquakes. Earth has a liquid outer core that generates a magnetosphere capable of deflecting most of the destructive solar winds and cosmic radiation."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2d/Meteosat-12-fci-march-equinox-2025-noon.jpg/330px-Meteosat-12-fci-march-equinox-2025-noon.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Earth","wikidata":"Q2"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/Tilling_with_Hungarian_Grey_cattles.tif/lossy-page1-500px-Tilling_with_Hungarian_Grey_cattles.tif.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/Tilling_with_Hungarian_Grey_cattles.tif/lossy-page1-1280px-Tilling_with_Hungarian_Grey_cattles.tif.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/Tilling_with_Hungarian_Grey_cattles.tif/lossy-page1-500px-Tilling_with_Hungarian_Grey_cattles.tif.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Tilling with Hungarian Grey cattle","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATilling_with_Hungarian_Grey_cattles.tif"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/90/Arr%C3%B2s%2C_sequer_%2826462086444%29.jpg/500px-Arr%C3%B2s%2C_sequer_%2826462086444%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/90/Arr%C3%B2s%2C_sequer_%2826462086444%29.jpg/1280px-Arr%C3%B2s%2C_sequer_%2826462086444%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/90/Arr%C3%B2s%2C_sequer_%2826462086444%29.jpg/500px-Arr%C3%B2s%2C_sequer_%2826462086444%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Rice tillage. Valencian Museum of Ethnology.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AArr%C3%B2s%2C_sequer_(26462086444).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8d/2DU_Kenya115_%285366706027%29.jpg/500px-2DU_Kenya115_%285366706027%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8d/2DU_Kenya115_%285366706027%29.jpg/1280px-2DU_Kenya115_%285366706027%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8d/2DU_Kenya115_%285366706027%29.jpg/500px-2DU_Kenya115_%285366706027%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A Kenyan farmer holding tilled soil","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A2DU_Kenya115_(5366706027).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2d/The_Mysterious_Case_of_the_Disappearing_Dust.jpg/500px-The_Mysterious_Case_of_the_Disappearing_Dust.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2d/The_Mysterious_Case_of_the_Disappearing_Dust.jpg/1280